\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS-Crown set to end 2022 stronger, forint holds near 400 to the euro\b0\par\par\uc2 835 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2022\par 12:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Jason Hovet\par        PRAGUE, Dec 30 (Reuters) - The Czech crown edged up to a\par fresh 10-month high on Friday, while Hungary's forint hung\par around the psychological 400-per-euro level as it sought to end\par the year on a strong note after a turbulent 2022.\par     Central Europe's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  diverged in 2022, with the crown\par faring the best after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  started market\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in May to prevent a plunge in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . It\par also ended interest rate hikes just as global central banks\par started tightening.\par     Hungary's forint has lost the most this year, hurt by\par soaring energy prices after Russia's invasion of Ukraine, and\par Budapest's ongoing disputes with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  over\par rule-of-law issues that have held up funds from Brussels. \par     The forint is due for a more than 7% fall in 2022, after\par recovering from sharper losses that had pushed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to a\par record low of 434.40 to the euro in October.\par     While a deal with Brussels over \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  funds on Dec. 12 has\par helped the forint, analysts still do not see next year's\par expected gains offsetting 2022's drop.\par     The forint was down 0.1% at 400.35 to the euro in\par mid-morning trade on Friday.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Erste Group Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a Dec. 23 outlook note that the\par eventual flow of EU funds and a positive turn in the current\par account balance amid easing energy prices would benefit the\par forint, pushing it further below 400.\par     "These improvements could give some room to maneuver to the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and decrease the inflation and yield path," it\par said.\par     On the other side, the Czech crown was at its strongest\par since before the Ukraine conflict started in February and has\par posted a 3% rise this year. \par     "We expect a roughly stability of the crown in the coming\par months," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ceska Sporitelna\f28 \uc2 \f2  analyst Jiri Polansky said. \par     "On one hand, a global economy weakening and expected\par stability of (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) rates should stop strengthening\par tendencies. But on the other hand, the (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) remains\par ready to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which is an important psychological factor\par for markets."\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's zloty edged down on Friday in slow\par holiday trade. It has lost 2% in 2022. Romania's leu\par was also steady, on course to end 2022 where it started.\par     Markets are set to continue watching central banks as they\par push down inflation at double-digit rates. But policymakers\par around central Europe look to be finished with heavy hiking\par cycles, which ran earlier than global peers such as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par                    CEE      SNAPSHO   AT                      \par                    MARKETS  T        1127              \par                                      CET               \par                             \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENC\f28 \b0 \highligh