\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS-Crown firms after  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market\b0\par\par\uc2 878 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par 11:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Anita Komuves\par     BUDAPEST, March 4 (Reuters) - The Czech crown gained on\par Friday and the Polish zloty firmed briefly after both their\par central banks \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to shore up the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as CEE markets were again hammered by the latest\par news on Russia's invasion of Ukraine.\par     Central European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have been hit hard by the war in\par Ukraine as investors flee to safer assets, pushing central banks\par in the Czech Republic and Poland into action to cap their\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ' losses. \par     A fire at Europe's biggest nuclear power station in Ukraine\par had sent world financial markets tumbling earlier. The fire was\par extinguished and officials said the plant was operating\par normally, after being seized by Russian forces.\par \par     The Czech crown was up 0.64% on the day, trading\par at 25.635 per euro after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it was in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market and was acting to mitigate excessive\par fluctuations.\par     The Polish zloty was still 0.68% weaker on the day\par and trading at 4.8360 to the euro, after some gains earlier in\par the morning.\par     A source close to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  told Reuters\par the bank was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a move coordinated with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Hungarian forint traded at 382.00 per euro,\par down 0.47% from Thursday, after hitting another record low at\par 383 earlier in the day.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of Hungary\f28 \uc2 \f2  delivered its biggest rate hike\par since 2008 on Thursday when it raised its one-week deposit rate,\par used to tackle short-term market volatility, by 75 basis points\par to 5.35%.\par     Like the crown and zloty, the forint pulled back from its\par deep losses, but some analysts said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might need\par to do more to shore up the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  did not achieve a significant change in\par the forint's rate with yesterday's hike of the one-week deposit\par rate," brokerage Equilor wrote.\par     On Friday the NBH reiterated that it was ready to act to\par ensure the stability of the local financial market.\par     In a Reuters poll on Friday analysts predicted an uncertain\par path to recovery for CEE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the next 12 months. \par     The forint was seen as recovering the slowest among peers\par while the Czech crown and Polish zloty were expected to recover\par to levels on par with previous forecasts from a month ago.\par \par     Stocks in the region fell, with Bucharest leading losses as\par it was down 5.14%. Budapest's equities were 1.91% lower. \par     Hungary's \f28 \uc2 \f2 OTP Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's shares were down 1.27% by\par 0959 GMT. The bank reported fourth-quarter profit that missed\par expectations and its CEO told a news conference that the bank\par planned to stay in Russia and Ukraine for the long term. OTP's\par stock lost about a third of its value since Russia invaded\par neighbouring Ukraine.\par     \par     \par                   CEE      SNAPSH   AT                   \par                   MARKETS  OT      1057            \par                                    CET             \par                            CURREN                        \par                            CIES                    \par                            Latest  Previo  Daily   Change\par                                    us              \par                            bid     close   change  in\par                                                    2022\par  EURCZK  Czech    <EURCZK  25.635  25.800   +0.64  -2.98%\par  =       crown    =>            0       0       %  \par  EURHUF  Hungary  <EURHUF  382.00  380.21  -0.47%  -3.30%\par  =       forint   =>           00      00          \par  EURPLN  Polish   <EURPLN  4.8360  4.8030  -0.68%  -5.07%\par  =       zloty    =>                               \par  EURRON  Romania  <EURRON  4.9490  4.9490   +0.00  -0.02%\par  =       n leu    =>                            %  \par  EURHRK  Croatia  <EURHRK  7.5610  7.5625   +0.02  -0.58%\par  =       n kuna   =>                            %  \par  EURRSD  Serbian  <EURRSD  117.55  117.65   +0.09   +0.03\par  =       dinar    =>           00      00       %       %\par          Note:    calculated from          1800          \par          daily                             CET     \par          change                                    \par                                                          \par                            Latest  Previo  Daily   Change\par                                    us              \par                                    close   change  in\par                                                    2022\par  .PX     Prague            1323.3  1364.2  -3.00%     \par                                 5     900          \par  .BUX    