\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-\uc2 Polish finance ministry\uc2  to exchange most funds on  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  market\b0\par\par\uc2 235 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par 14:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds details)\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, March 2 (Reuters) - Poland will exchange most of its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds on the market, the finance ministry said on Wednesday, after the zloty \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit its weakest level since 2009.\par \par \uc2 In common with other central and eastern European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the zloty has weakened significantly since Russia invaded Ukraine, as investors ditch riskier assets. The finance ministry's decision will support the zloty exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  informs that the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds at its disposal will be exchanged primarily on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on an appropriate scale," the ministry said in a statement. "The exchange of these funds at the \uc2 National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) will be of a complementary nature."\par \par \uc2 The NBP \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, buying zlotys after it said the recent depreciation was not in line with the Polish economy's fundamentals and that it was ready to react to excessive moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, this did little to halt the zloty's slide, as it weakened to a 13-year low of 4.8335 against the euro on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pared its losses slightly after the finance ministry's annoucement and at 1307 GMT it was down 1.35% on the day at 4.8077. (Reporting by Alan Charlish, Pawel Florkiewicz, Anna Wlodarczak-Semczuk) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-3-2T14:14:48.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220302ei3202sru\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
