\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS-Zloty weakens to level seen as possible  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  trigger\b0\par\par\uc2 786 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2021\par 11:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Feb 11 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty retreated back\par above 4.50 to the euro on Thursday, a level that economists have\par said could trigger an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in\par December to weaken the zloty when it was moving in the opposite\par direction, with markets seeing 4.50 as its preferred level. \par     However on Friday last week, Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Adam Glapinski\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par stressed that the bank did not have a target for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par prompting it to move further below the 4.50 level.\par     "This is something we will probably see in the next few\par weeks, EUR/PLN will fluctuate near the level of 4.50 due to this\par expectation of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,"\par said Krystian Jaworski, senior economist at Credit Agricole in\par Warsaw.\par     At 1004 GMT the zloty was 0.30% weaker against the euro at\par 4.5036.\par     Marcin Sulewski, an economist at Santander Bank Polska, said\par there could be profit-taking on the zloty and the Czech crown\par  after their recent stong run.\par     The crown, which hit an 11-month high on Wednesday, was\par 0.14% weaker at 25.81. It has been boosted by speculation over\par rate hikes later this year in the Czech Republic, which analysts\par say may be the first country in the region to raise borrowing\par costs.\par     Markets were looking ahead to Czech inflation data due on\par Friday. "Higher inflation versus estimates would likely boost\par interest rate (markets), which could strengthen the crown in the\par short-term," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Komercni Banka\f28 \uc2 \f2  said.\par     The Hungarian forint was little changed at 356.74.\par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been moving in a range between 355 and 361 in\par the past weeks, having tested but not significantly broken the\par 200-day moving average near 355.\par     "In the past two days we saw a negative correction in the\par euro-forint exchange rate which brought the rate closer to the\par 200-day moving average again," brokerage Equilor wrote in a\par morning note.\par     Stocks were mixed, with the main indexes in Budapest\par and Warsaw up 1.19% and 1.11% respectively, while in\par Prague the PX index was down 0.18%.\par     In Warsaw shares in e-commerce group Allegro rose\par more than 7% at one point, bouncing back after a sharp fall so\par far this year.\par \par                    CEE       SNAPSHO   AT                       \par                    MARKETS   T        1104 CET           \par                              \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENC\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                             \par                              IES                         \par                              Latest   Previous  Daily    Change\par                              bid      close     change   in 2021\par  EURCZK=  Czech    <EURCZK=  25.8100   25.7750   -0.14%   +1.62%\par           crown    >                                     \par  EURHUF=  Hungary  <EURHUF=  356.740  356.9500   +0.06%   +1.68%\par           forint   >               0                     \par  EURPLN=  Polish   <EURPLN=