\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS-Czech crown hovers near 11-month high ahead of c.bank meeting\b0\par\par\uc2 756 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2021\par 11:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Alan Charlish and Jason Hovet\par     WARSAW, Feb 4 (Reuters) - The Czech crown was flat\par on Thursday, but was trading  near a 11-month high, ahead of a\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meeting which is expected to give clues on the\par future path of interest rates.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  is likely to keep policy settings\par unchanged at a meeting on Thursday, a Reuters poll showed on\par Tuesday, but a majority of analysts now see the bank raising\par interest rates by the end of the year.\par     "The market does not expect any policy rate change and\par neither do we, but the new forecast and the presser will shed\par more light on the policy rate trajectory, mainly in the second\par half in 2021 and beyond," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Komercni Banka\f28 \uc2 \f2  rates trader Marek\par Lesko said in a client note.\par     Central bankers have already signalled chances of a rise in\par the key rate from the current level of 0.25%, and markets are\par pricing in expectations of a hike later in 2021. \par     At 0921 GMT, the crown was flat against the euro at 25.90,\par hovering around its highest level since March 2020 at 25.88,\par which it hit earlier in the week.\par     The Polish zloty was down 0.16% at 4.492, after\par breaking through the 4.50 level that economists say could\par trigger a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier in the week.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (NBP) kept its main interest\par rate on hold at a record low of 0.1% on Wednesday and reiterated\par that it may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to weaken the\par zloty.\par      "Even though the threat of an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may not be\par imminent everyone has to consider the risk of such an action,"\par said Piotr Poplawski, senior economist at ING in Warsaw.\par     The Hungarian forint slipped 0.18% to 355.13. The\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been hovering at this level, its 200-day moving\par average, since Tuesday.    \par     "The forint is waiting. The euro-forint rate is still at the\par key 200-day moving average level, which is expected to stop the\par short-term forint strengthening trend," brokerage Equilor wrote\par in a note.\par     \par                      CEE       SNAPSHO   AT                       \par                      MARKETS   T        1021 CET           \par                                \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENC\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                             \par                                IES                         \par                                Latest   Previous  Daily    Change\par                                bid      close     change   in 2021\par  EURCZK=  Czech      <EURCZK=  25.9000   25.8980   -0.01%   +1.27%\par           crown      >                                     \par  EURHUF=  Hungary    <EURHUF=  355.760  355.1300   -0.18%   +1.96%\par           forint     >               0                     \par  EURPLN=  Polish     <EURPLN=   4.4920    4.4850   -0.16%   +1.50%\par           zloty      >                                     \par  EURRON=  Romanian   <EURRON=   4.8740    4.8750   +0.02%   -0.18%\par           leu        >                                     \par  EURHRK=  Croatian   <EURHRK=   7.5660    7.5675   +0.02%   -0.25%\par           kuna       >     