\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS-Forint outperforms peers as PM's aide expect fast economic recovery\b0\par\par\uc2 751 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 2021\par 11:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Anita Komuves\par     BUDAPEST, Jan 20 (Reuters) - Central European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par edged up on Wednesday, with the Hungarian forint outperforming\par its peers and extending gains from the previous session when the\par prime minister's aide said the country's economy could recover\par quickly.\par     The forint gained 0.28% and was trading at 357.00,\par breaking out of the tight 359-362 range it has traded for more\par than a week.\par     "The comments by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Marton Nagy\f28 \uc2 \f2  yesterday made markets a bit\par more optimistic, and the slight weakening of the dollar also\par helps," a Budapest-based \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader said.\par     Hungary's economy could recover rapidly once restrictions to\par contain the COVID-19 pandemic end and the economy could expand\par by 5% to 6% this year, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Marton Nagy\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Viktor Orban\f28 \uc2 \f2 's senior\par economic aide said.\par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the zloty in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the\par surprise rate cut by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Romanian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could be helping\par the forint strengthen more than we expected," another trader in\par Budapest said.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Romania cut its benchmark interest rate\par by a quarter-point to 1.25% on Friday. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungary's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  held main interest rates unchanged last month and\par has pledged a cautious monetary policy.\par     The leu edged down 0.02%, trading at 4.8750 per\par euro.\par     The zloty firmed 0.18% and was trading at 4.5235\par versus the common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reiterated its\par dovish stance. \par     Uncertainty over the COVID-19 pandemic raises a slight risk\par of further rates cuts in Poland and they are more likely to stay\par stable as the economy recovers, central banker Cezary Kochalski\par said. \par     The Czech economy is headed for a double-dip recession due\par to the pandemic but the second dip is likely to be shallower\par than the first, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Jiri Rusnok said on\par Tuesday. \par     He reiterated that the bank did not feel a need to ease\par monetary policy further.\par     The Czech crown was up 0.05% and trading at 26.133\par per euro.\par     Stock markets in the region were mixed, with Budapest's\par equities weakening 0.53% while Warsaw was up\par 0.18%. Prague firmed 0.29%.\par     \par                     CEE       SNAPSHO   AT                      \par                     MARKETS   T        1048 CET          \par                               \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENC\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                            \par                               IES                        \par                               Latest   Previous  Daily   Change\par                               bid      close     change  in 2021\par  EURCZK=  Czech     <EURCZK=  26.1330   26.1460   +0.05   +0.37%\par           crown     >                                 %  \par  EURHUF=  Hungary   <EURHUF=  357.000  358.0000   +0.28   +1.60%\par           forint    >               0                 %  \par  EURPLN=  Polish    <EURPLN=   4.52