\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Polish c.bank holds rates steady, but says  \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions \highlight\uc2  possible\b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2021\par 16:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, details)\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Jan 13 (Reuters) - The \uc2 National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) said on Wednesday that it may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to help support the economy, after it decided to leave its main interest rate unchanged at 0.1%.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly said that the strength of the Polish zloty could threaten Poland's economic recovery from the COVID-19 pandemic, and governor \uc2 Adam Glapinski\uc2  confirmed in a recent interview that it had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "In order to strengthen the impact of NBP's monetary policy easing on the economy, NBP may also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fears, Polish exports have posted robust growth and the economy has proved more resilient to the COVID-19 pandemic than many others.\par \par \uc2 Glapinski startled economists in December when excerpts of an interview were published in which he said rate cuts were possible in the first quarter. However, in the full text, which appeared in January, he also said that in the baseline scenario rates would stay on hold.\par \par \uc2 "The full content of the interview with the \uc2 National Bank of Poland\uc2  (NBP) governor indicated that stable interest rates is still the most likely scenario. So the result of the January Monetary Policy Council (MPC) meeting is not a surprise," said Piotr Bielski, director of the economic analysis department at \uc2 Santander Bank Polska\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Poland's benchmark interest rate has been at a record low of 0.1% since rate-setters slashed the cost of borrowing three times by a cumulative 140 basis points during the first wave of the economically damaging COVID-19 pandemic in spring.\par \par \uc2 Of 21 analysts polled by Reuters, 19 had expected rates to remain on hold.\par \par \uc2 The Polish zloty, which had been broadly stable throughout the day, started to weaken after the release of The NBP's statement, and was 0.20% softer on the day at 1533 GMT. (Reporting by Alan Charlish, Pawel Florkiewicz, Anna Koper and Justyna Pawlak Editing by Mark Heinrich, William Maclean) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-1-13T16:45:14.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210113eh1d02iqp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
