\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  ease as dollar firms, stocks climb to pre-pandemic levels\b0\par\par\uc2 806 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2021\par 11:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Anita Komuves\par     BUDAPEST, Jan 11 (Reuters) - Central European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par slid on Monday as the dollar was strengthening in a risk-off\par mood as investors were concerned about rising coronavirus cases\par and political risks in the United States. \par     Democratic lawmakers in the U.S are trying to impeach\par President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  to bar him from running for office again.\par  \par     Markets were also paying attention to Poland, where the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  holds its rate-setting meeting on Wednesday. \par     Rates are expected to stay on hold, but governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Adam\par Glapinski\f28 \uc2 \f2  recently said that a rate cut could be possible in the\par first quarter, which introduced an element of uncertainty.\par  \par     Lower-than-expected inflation reported last week also\par increased the likelihood of a rate cut, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  wrote. \par     Flash CPI was up 2.3% year-on-year in December while\par analysts polled by Reuters had expected 2.60%. \par     The zloty slid 0.41% on Monday to 4.5260 per euro.\par     "Due to possible re-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , it seems that in the\par coming days the EUR/PLN rate will remain above 4.50," \f28 \uc2 \f2 PKO BP\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par wrote in a note. \par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in\par December to weaken the zloty to help exports.\par     Elsewhere, the Czech crown was down 0.31% and\par trading at 26.215 while the Hungarian forint eased\par 0.25% to 360.60 versus the euro. \par     "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the region are softening this morning, and\par the direction from American investors later in the day will\par decide where they finish the day," a Budapest-based \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader\par said. "The impeachment carries political risks."\par     Hungary's preliminary December budget deficit surged to a\par record 2.25 trillion forints ($7.59 billion) due to sharply\par increased spending before the end of the year, boosting the 2020\par deficit to 5.549 trillion forints, the Finance Ministry said on\par Monday.\par     The ministry said Hungary's 2020 budget deficit could come\par in at around 9% of GDP, the top of its latest upgraded forecast,\par showing the extent of the blow to the economy from the\par coronavirus pandemic.\par     Stocks in the region firmed, with equities in Prague, Warsaw\par and Budapest extending their gains to levels that are the\par strongest since February 2020, before the coronavirus and\par lockdowns hit economies in the region.\par     Equities in Warsaw gained 0.81% while they were up\par 0.36% in Prague and edged up 0.07% in Budapest.\par     \par     \par                     CEE      SNAPSHO   AT                       \par                     MARKETS  T        1116 CET           \par                              \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENC\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                             \par                              IES                         \par                              Latest   Previous  Daily    Change\par                              bid      close     change   in 2021\par  EURCZK=  Czech     <EURCZK  26.2150   26.1350   -0.31%   +0.05%\par 