\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4- \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 's c.bank chief says rate cuts,  \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions \highlight\uc2  possible\b0\par\par\uc2 428 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2020\par 16:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds another rate-setter's comment)\par \par \uc2 By Alan Charlish and Anna Koper\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Dec 30 (Reuters) - \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could cut interest rates during the first quarter of next year and may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the zloty, the bank's governor said, undermining previous expectations for stable borrowing costs until 2022.\par \par \uc2 The comments on rate cuts, which appeared in excerpts late on Tuesday on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and on the financial news website Obserwator Finansowy, ran counter to statements governor \uc2 Adam Glapinski\uc2  made as recently as this month that rates would remain at a record low of 0.1% for a long time.\par \par \uc2 "The current level of interest rates is appropriate and best suits the current situation," Glapinski said.\par \par \uc2 "However, in the first quarter of next year, further rate cuts are possible," he added. "We are conducting the appropriate analyses of the possible circumstances and potential effects of such a reduction at the NBP (\uc2 National Bank of Poland\uc2 )."\par \par \uc2 Analysts polled by Reuters earlier in December expected rates to hold steady until the fourth quarter of 2022.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, other bankers from the 10-strong rate-setting panel leant weight to the possibility of a cut and \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Central banker Jerzy Zyzynski told Reuters a cut to zero was possible in the first quarter, citing a "sluggish" recovery.\par \par \uc2 Fellow rate-setter Rafal Sura told the Polish agency PAP further cuts could not be ruled out in the future, although he did not currently see a need.\par \par \uc2 PAP also quoted rate-setter Grazyna Ancyparowicz as saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have to cut rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market simultaneously if the zloty continued to strengthen.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 In an excerpt published on Wednesday, Glapinski said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the zloty to help exports and boost the economic recovery from the COVID-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Already, on Dec. 18, a source close to the bank said it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the zloty.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday afternoon, the zloty weakened by as much as 1.77%, causing speculation of a further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Reuters was unable to confirm if the bank had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The recent pressure to increase the value of the zloty is very worrying and very damaging," Glapinski was quoted as saying.\par \par \uc2 "With our inflation projections at a low level next year, this obviously creates room for possible decisive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." (Reporting by Alan Charlish; Editing by Clarence Fernandez, Simon Cameron-Moore, Steve Orlofsky and Barbara Lewis) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-12-30T16:55:03.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201230egcu00hld\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
