\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  an option if Polish zloty too strong - c.banker Lon\b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2020\par 11:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Aug 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the strength of the Polish zloty threatens exports, rate-setter Eryk Lon said in a column published on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Some market participants have already speculated the \uc2 Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could act to weaken the zloty after it said in June the economic recovery could be "mitigated by the lack of a visible zloty exchange rate adjustment to the global pandemic shock".\par \par \uc2 "In the event of any threats to the profitability of Polish exports, I consider it advisable to use...(\b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), which should then boil down to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  taking actions aimed at a possible weakening of the zloty," Lon wrote in an article for the website of Catholic radio station \uc2 Radio Maryja\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The zloty has firmed around 5% since hitting an 11-year low in late March, in the early stages of the COVID-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Poland has cut interest rates three times by a cumulative 140 basis points since the novel coronavirus reached the country in March, bringing the main rate to a record low of 0.1%.\par \par \uc2 In his article for \uc2 Radio Maryja\uc2 , Lon reiterated his view rates should remain on hold this year and probably next year too.\par \par \uc2 He also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should consider widening its inflation target range to 2.5% plus or minus two percentage points from the current range of 2.5% plus or minus one percentage point.\par \par \uc2 "I think that what is of key importance, above all, is the assumption that Poland as an emerging country has a right to slightly higher inflation than mature countries," he said. (Reporting by Alan Charlish and Anna Koper; editing by Barbara Lewis) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-8-11T10:13:37.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200811eg8b01gjq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
