\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED-CEE MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  weaken, \uc2 Hungarian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  seen holding fire\b0\par\par\uc2 763 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2018\par 13:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Corrects par 5 to November inflation not December)\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to keep rates at record\par lows\par     * Hungarian 10-year bond spread over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  widens further\par     * Kuna sets December low after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par \par     By Sandor Peto\par     BUDAPEST, Dec 18 (Reuters) - Central European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par eased before a meeting of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that's\par expected to keep its benchmark interest rate at a record-low 0.9\par percent.\par     Many investors expect the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  to signal an\par economic slowdown at its Dec. 18-19 meeting, but Tuesday's\par Polish data showed continued fast growth in wages were not\par expected to lead to a more hawkish monetary policy stance in\par Warsaw, either. \par     Central European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  including the forint\par and the zloty slipped against the euro, falling less\par than 0.1 percent by 0948 GMT in slow trade.\par     Some analysts have said the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may\par provide markets with some clues about a slow monetary tightening\par next year.\par     A bigger-than-expected retreat in annual headline inflation\par to 3.1 percent in November has reduced the likelihood of hawkish\par comments from the meeting, dealers said.\par     A fixed income trader said rate setters "can sit back" after\par a decline in crude prices in the fourth quarter.\par     "I do not think that they will issue any hawkish comment,"\par the trader said.\par     Hungarian government bond yields as well as yields in\par interest rate swaps and forward rate agreements extended\par Monday's rebound after a sharp decline in recent months.\par     The yield of the 10-year government bond at 3.26 percent\par offered the highest spread over the corresponding Polish yield\par for over a month.\par     The Polish 10-year yield, which had fallen less\par in the past months, tracked a fall in Bunds and U.S. Treasuries,\par and at 2.888 percent it set a new two-year low.\par     The Czech 10-year yield, bid at 1.948 percent, was flat.\par     A recent decline in Czech market yields has mis-priced the\par magnitude of likely further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate increases, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe\par Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts said in a note.\par     The bank could keep rates on hold at its meeting on\par Thursday, but its "statement might be more hawkish than the\par market currently expects given the relatively weak CZK (crown)\par and ever strengthening demand pressures to inflation," they\par said.\par     The kuna traded at its weakest levels this month,\par at 7.405 versus the euro, off last week's five-month highs. \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Croatia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought 458 million euros on Monday in its\par second big market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in December.\par     \par             CEE       SNAPSHOT   AT                         \par             MARKETS             1048 CET            \par                       \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRE