\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS-Zloty steadies under shadow of Polish political turmoil\b0\par\par\uc2 802 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juli 2017\par 11:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Zloty steadies despite uncertainties over Polish reform\par     * Forint retreats behind key 305 line versus euro\par     * Czech crown stuck at 26/euro, rate hike possible\par \par     By Sandor Peto\par     BUDAPEST, July 25 (Reuters) - The zloty steadied\par on Tuesday following recent jitters prompted by political\par wrangling over reforms which increase Poland's right-wing\par government's influence over the judiciary.\par     Poland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traded steady at 4.2545 versus the euro at\par 0847 GMT, while other Central European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were mixed as\par investors await clues over global interest rate trends from the\par Fed's two-day meeting on Tuesday and Wednesday.\par     The zloty rebounded from 3-month lows hit on Monday, after\par President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Andrzej Duda\f28 \uc2 \f2  unexpectedly announced that he would veto\par two of three reform bills passed by parliament which determine\par the make-up of the Supreme Court.\par     The eurosceptic Law and Justice party's (PiS) reforms have\par triggered nationwide street protests and threats of \f28 \uc2 \f2 European\par Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  sanctions. \par     Duda had been seen as an ally of PiS and his \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par also caused uncertainty over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's domestic politics,\par including some speculation of early elections.\par     However, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rebounded in the morning session as\par market analysts dismissed the likelihood of this.\par     "To the extent to which PLN weakened yesterday afternoon due\par to speculation over early parliamentary elections, this weakness\par should partly reverse today," ING said in a note, adding that\par the rebound could help the leu.\par     The Polish presidential veto does not remove political\par uncertainty weighing on Polish asset prices, analysts said.\par     "We would simply regard this as a breather for the zloty\par given that the ruling PiS party will likely not back down from\par its policies easily," Raiffeisen analyst Wolfgang Ernst said in\par a note.\par     "The next relevant date for PLN movement should now be on\par Wednesday when the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  will meet to discuss the topic," he added.\par     The forint, meanwhile, eased slightly, retreating\par from 305 against the euro, which it briefly crossed on Monday\par after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pumped additional liquidity\par into interbank markets through its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 fx\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap tenders.\par     But dealers said the forint's retreat was caused by\par technical reasons rather than the tenders as it had become\par oversold against the euro, while it was also giving up some of\par its gains in its zloty cross.\par     "It is justified if the forint outperforms the zloty now...\par but its firming seems to have lost steam," one Budapest-based\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealer said.\par     The Czech crown continued to hover on the weak\par side of the 26 line against the euro, firmer from Monday, with\par some investors expecting the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to start to lift\par interest rates on Aug. 3, for the first time in almost a decade.\par   \par                 CEE MARKETS  SNAPSH   AT  1047 CET         \par              