\par\par \b \uc2 *Polish President's Aide Lopinski: New  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Loans Bill Beneficial For Borrowers\b0\par\par\uc2 727 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2016\par 11:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:05 ET *Lopinski: Draft Of New \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Loans Bill Signed By President, Will Be Sent To Parliament\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:05 ET *Lopinski: Poland's New \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Loans Draft Affects \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Spreads\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:06 ET *Lopinski: Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Loans Draft To Allow For Negotiated Mortgage Conversion\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:08 ET *Lopinski: Polish Regulators To Create Incentives For Banks To Convert \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Loans\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:09 ET *\uc2 Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chief Glapinski: \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Mortgage Loans No Risk For Stability\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:10 ET *Glapinski: But \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  Has Reasons To \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  As \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Loans May Pose Long-Term Risks\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:11 ET *Glapinski: New \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Loans Draft Won't Destabilize Polish Banks\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:11 ET *Poland's Glapinski: Asked President To Abandon Plan To Convert \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Loans\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:12 ET *Poland's Glapinski: One-Time \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Loans Conversion Impossible At This Time\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:12 ET *Poland's Glapinski: \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Loans Conversion Should, Will Happen Eventually\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:12 ET *Poland's Glapinski: Banks To Negotiate \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Loans Conversion With Customers\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:13 ET *Poland's Glapinski: Regulator To Create Conditions Making \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Loans Unprofitable For Banks\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:13 ET *Poland's Glapinski: \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Loans Conversion To Be Gradual, Won't Undermine Stability\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:14 ET *Poland's Glapinski: \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Loans Conversion To Take Some Time But Not Too Long\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:14 ET *Poland's Glapinski: Zloty Remains Strongly Undervalued, Should Rise\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:18 ET *Poland's Glapinski: Regulator To Increase Costs For Banks With \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Loans Portfolio\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:19 ET *Poland's Glapinski: Regulator To Increase Capital Adequacy Requirement For Banks With \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Loans\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:21 ET *Poland's Glapinski: Regulator Has Legal Tools For Gradual \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Loans Conversion\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:39 ET *Poland's Lopinski: If Negotiated \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Approach Fails, Ready To Return To Mandatory Conversion Plan\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:41 ET *\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Spreads Bill To Cost Banks PLN3.6B-PLN4B - Polish President's Official\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:43 ET *Glapinski: Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Guards Stability, Guards Zloty Value\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:43 ET *Glapinski: \uc2 Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Policy Unchanged Re Stability, Zloty\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:50 ET *Glapinski: Poland Interest Rates To Stay Unchanged In Coming Quarters, Seems Obvious\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 05:59 ET *Glapinski: Poland New \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Loans Rules For Banks May Be Ready In Oct\par \par \uc2 2 Aug 2016 06:04 ET  Poland to Phase Out \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Loans, Plans Gradual Conversion Into Zloty\par \par \uc2 WARSAW--Poland's president postponed his earlier plan to enforce a conversion of foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans into zloty-denominated loans. Instead, the country's financial regulator will increase costs for banks that refuse to convert such loans into zloty, in an effort to gradually phase them out, officials said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, Adam Glapinski, said the country's regulator will significantly increase capital adequacy requirements for banks with foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans portfolios, creating incentives to negotiate a conversion with borrowers.\par \par \uc2 Under earlier proposals, banks were supposed to convert the loans into zloty-denominated products at historical exchange rates, in a move that would likely cause massive losses and could destabilize the Polish banking sector.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Glapinski said the new approach is safe for the sector and spread over time. He didn't give details but said the period of time he had in mind wasn't very long.\par \par \uc2 Presidential aide Maciej Lopinski said if banks fail to move to convert the loans voluntarily, in a year Poland will revisit its plan for an automatic conversion at a historical exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans became a problem for many Polish borrowers when the zloty tumbled amid the global financial crisis in 2009. It also became a political issue during last year's presidential and parliamentary campaigns, leading to promises by the socially conservative camp, which won both elections, that it would deal with the matter once in power.\par \par \uc2 Write to Martin M. Sobczyk at martin.sobczyk@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 02, 2016 06:04 ET (10:04 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160802ec8200134\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
