\par\par \b \uc2 Poland - Factors to Watch July 11\b0\par\par\uc2 399 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2016\par 08:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Following are news stories, press reports and events to watch that may affect Poland's financial markets on Monday. ALL TIMES GMT (Poland: GMT + 2 hours):\par \par \uc2 DATA\par \par \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to publish its newest inflation projection at 0700 GMT.\par \par \uc2 The statistics office is scheduled to publish consumer price index (CPI) data for June at 1200 GMT.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNMENT\par \par \uc2 Jaroslaw Kaczynski, head of the ruling Law and Justice (PiS) party, told daily Rzeczpospolita he would strive to become prime minister only if he thought something bad was going on in the government, and it is not so at the moment. He also signalled a need for change in the foreign ministry without elaborating.\par \par \uc2 FINANCE MINISTRY\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Ministry\uc2  sees no need for an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, as the post-Brexit shock proved not that great and the situation is stabilising, Finance Minister Pawel Szalamacha reiterated in his interview for Do Rzeczy weekly.\par \par \uc2 PZU\par \par \uc2 The head of Poland's state-run insurer PZU, Michal Krupinski, reiterated in his interview for the wSieci weekly that he is ready for talks with any Polish bank owner wanting to sell.\par \par \uc2 PKP CARGO\par \par \uc2 Poland's rail freight carrier \uc2 PKP Cargo\uc2  is ready to reinitiate talks with fellow state-run oil refiner \uc2 PKN Orlen\uc2  on buying PKN's oil transport unit Koltrans, \uc2 PKP Cargo\uc2 's chief executive Maciej Libiszewski told daily Gazeta Polska Codziennie.\par \par \uc2 ASSECO POLSKA\par \par \uc2 Eastern Europe's largest software maker, \uc2 Asseco Poland\uc2 , aims at becoming the global player on the e-signature market, its chief executive Adam Goral told daily Puls Biznesu.\par \par \uc2 STATE FUNDS\par \par \uc2 Pawel Borys, head of Poland's state-run PFR fund, told wSieci weekly that the assets controlled by the country's Demografic Reserve Fund (FRD) should be raised to 150-200 billion zlotys.\par \par \uc2 NETIA\par \par \uc2 Poland's No. 2 telecoms operator Netia came under attack from hackers who may have stolen the data of some of its clients, a company spokeswoman said on Friday evening.\par \par \uc2 \f2 ****Reuters has not verified these stories and does not\par vouch for their accuracy.****\par               \par               \par For other related news, double click on:\par  Polish equities           E.Europe equities     \par  Polish money              Polish debt           \par  Eastern Europe             All emerging markets  \par  Hot stocks                 Stock markets         \par  Market debt news           \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news            \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For real-time index quotes, double click on: Warsaw WIG20 Budapest BUX Prague PX \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-7-11T07:12:05.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160711ec7b00bqo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
