\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2  Ready to  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Market If Zloty Drops on Greek Crisis\b0\par\par\uc2 By Patryk Wasilewski   \par \uc2 202 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2015\par 14:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW--\b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance ministry\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  are ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakens as a result of the Greek crisis, Finance Minister Mateusz Szczurek said Monday.\par \par \uc2 The minister said the country's financial system and economy are robust and there is no risk to it from a potential exit by Greece from the single-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  area.\par \par \uc2 "We have...46 billion zlotys in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which means in case of significant weakening pressure, some speculative moves, both the ministry...and the \uc2 National Bank of Poland\uc2  can stabilize the situation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Mr. Szczurek said.\par \par \uc2 As well as the finance ministry's 46 billion zlotys ($12.5 billion) in cash reserves, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had 93.9 billion euros in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at the end of May.\par \par \uc2 The Polish zloty has strengthened this year and one euro now buys 4.18 zlotys, compared with 4.29 zlotys at the beginning of the year.\par \par \uc2 Write to Patryk Wasilewski at patryk.wasilewski@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 22, 2015 08:57 ET (12:57 GMT)