\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 1-Assets rangebound, all eyes on \uc2 Polish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 803 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 2015\par 11:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Poland seen keeping rates on hold at 1.5 pct\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  comments watched across region\par     * Zloty may extend rally if \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ignores its\par strength\par \par     By Sandor Peto and Jakub Iglewski\par     BUDAPEST, April 15 (Reuters) - The zloty firmed slightly on\par Wednesday as investors awaited the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par post-meeting press conference, and any comments from\par policymakers about the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent strength.\par     The bank is expected to keep its main rate at a record low\par 1.5 percent after it said last month's 50 basis point cut was\par the last in its easing cycle.\par     Investors across the region, however, will be watching the\par news conference at 1400 GMT, as any sign that rate setters are\par worried about the zloty's strength could provide clues about the\par chances of further monetary easing across the region.\par     The zloty firmed beyond the key 4.0 against the\par euro on Tuesday for the first time since August 2011. On\par Wednesday it was 0.1 percent stronger at 4.014 at 0755 GMT.\par     "The comments from Poland will be more important to us today\par than the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's comments (at a news conference\par later on Wednesday)," one Budapest-based fixed income trader\par said.\par     Other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the region were rangebound. The dinar\par  firmed a shade even though the Serbian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par was in the market selling dinars on Tuesday as its two rate cuts\par this year have failed to curb the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength.\par     Strong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hinder export growth and are keeping\par inflation too low, at around zero in the region.\par     A Reuters poll on Tuesday showed that analysts see little\par chance that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market\par to weaken the zloty. \par     "Given the long history of the MPC (Monetary Policy Council)\par ignoring the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength and factors supporting it, even\par a small departure from such a scenario (in the bank's comments\par today) may weaken the zloty," mBank analysts said in a note.    \par     "In a broader context, the appreciation is stable and\par steady, just as the fundamental factors that fuel it: a\par sustainable difference in real rates (premium over euro zone\par debt yields) and the building up of a cyclical upturn in the\par Polish economy," they added.  \par      On the other hand, the zloty may jump if the bank ignores\par the issue of its strength.\par      "If (the bank's chief) ... \f28 \uc2 \f2 Marek Belka\f28 \uc2 \f2  does not show any\par concern regarding the strengthening zloty ... the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may\par test the 3.95-3.98 per euro range this week," PKO \f28 \uc2 \f2 BP\f28 \uc2 \f2 's analyst\par Joanna Bachert said in a note. \par  *                                                     