\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Polish interest rates seen flat until hike in Q3 2016\b0\par\par\uc2 393 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2015\par 13:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * All 22 analysts see unchanged rates on April 15\par \par \uc2 * Analysts see first hike in Q3 2016 - median\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced end of rate cut cycle\par \par \uc2 * To see results in Eikon app click on reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/cb-polls and select "Poland"\par \par \uc2 By Marcin Goettig\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, April 10 (Reuters) - Poland is likely to keep interest rates unchanged until a hike in the second half of 2016, a Reuters poll showed on Friday.\par \par \uc2 All 22 economists polled from April 7 until April 10 expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council (MPC) to keep its benchmark rate at 1.50 percent when it meets on Tuesday and Wednesday next week.\par \par \uc2 On average, the poll gave a 97 percent chance that rates will remain unchanged next week.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced an end to its rate cut cycle after it cut rates by a larger-than-expected 50 basis points in March, bringing them to a new all-time low.\par \par \uc2 The median of forecasts showed analysts expect rates to rise in the third quarter of 2016, with the benchmark rate seen at 2.00 percent at the end of next year.\par \par \uc2 Poland's zloty \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a 3-1/2 year high of 4.002 against the euro earlier this week, boosted by the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive stimulus programme and the fact that Polish rates are still significantly higher than those in the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Mateusz Szczurek said on Thursday that so far the zloty's strength was not posing a threat to economic growth.\par \par \uc2 Some analyst expect that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may address the zloty strength at its post-meeting conference next week.\par \par \uc2 "I expect that we would have to see the zloty strengthen to below 4 to the euro to see a verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Piotr Kalisz, CEE economist at Citi's \uc2 Bank Handlowy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "A rapid strengthening to below 3.90 to the euro would increase the likelihood of an actual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Kalisz said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut its benchmark interest rate by a total 325 basis points since late 2012 to spur growth and inflation in central and eastern Europe's largest economy. (Editing by \uc2 Alison Williams\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-4-13T11:10:00.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150410eb4a00bf5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
