\par\par \b \uc2 Polish c.banker Chojna-Duch sceptical on rate cut expectations\b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 15:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, March 27 (Reuters) - Polish central banker Elzbieta Chojna-Duch said on Friday cutting interest rates may not always be effective at countering market turbulence, when asked about market expectations of a rate cut by year end to contain zloty gains.\par \par \uc2 The zloty hit its strongest level in more than two years against the euro earlier this week, leading traders to bet that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could lower rates further by year end to prevent excessive gains of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Asked about these expectations, Chojna-Duch, a member of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council, told Reuters:\par \par \uc2 "Interest rates are not always the right instrument to counter significant market turbulence," she said. "Lowering them in case of external turbulence may not always be expedient and effective."\par \par \uc2 Markets price in a roughly 60 percent chance that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will cut rates by a further 25 basis points by the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the bank's Monetary Policy Council ended a monetary-easing cycle.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, minutes from the March meeting showed the majority of rate setters still saw scope for an "adjustment" in rates in case of unexpected strong shocks to the Polish economy or the region.\par \par \uc2 The zloty traded at 4.0960 to the euro by 1418 GMT.\par \par \uc2 An alternative tool for containing zloty gains is for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The last \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt excessive zloty gains took place in April 2010, when the zloty reached levels of about 3.80 to the euro.\par \par \uc2 Analysts from \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 's Polish unit mBank said on Friday they expected the zloty to trade at 4.00 to the euro in two weeks given, among other things, the reluctance of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate-setters to cut rates further. (Reporting by Marcin Goettig; Editing by Christian Lowe) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-3-27T15:57:55.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150327eb3r00ix0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
