\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MARKETS 1-Dinar firms, low CPIs keep  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  fragile\b0\par\par\uc2 804 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 2015\par 10:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Serbia seen keeping rates on hold for now, dinar firms\par     * Crown eases again Czech president comments\par     * Inflation weighs on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Polish CPI due at 1300 GMT\par \par     By Sandor Peto\par     BUDAPEST, Jan 15 (Reuters) - Serbia's dinar firmed on\par Thursday ahead of a meeting of the Serbian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which\par is expected to keep interest rates on hold like \f28 \uc2 \f2 Poland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  did on Wednesday.\par     A renewed decline in the Czech crown indicated\par that speculation for more monetary easing in Central Europe was\par set to prevail, continuing to weigh on the region's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Those expectations have been were fuelled by December annual\par consumer price index (CPI) figures -- a low 0.1 percent in\par Prague and -0.9 percent in Hungary. Poland will publish its own\par data at 1300 GMT.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is widely expected to cut its record\par low interest rates further, a move which could trigger strong\par demand at the country's first bond auction this year on\par Thursday.\par     "(The) zloty can keep part of the gains against main\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but the risk of weakening after the CPI data is\par high," Pekao bank analysts said in a note, adding that bond\par yields could stay near record lows.\par     The zloty edged higher to 4.257 against the euro\par by 0853 GMT and Hungary's forint firmed a quarter of a\par percent. \par     The dinar firmed 0.1 percent to 122.47, still\par staying near record lows even though it extended Wednesday's\par gains as companies were selling euros to cover VAT payments due\par on Jan. 15.\par     Serbia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , worried about the fragility of the\par dinar, is seen keeping rates on hold on Thursday.\par  \par     "Despite recent headwinds, we reaffirm our bullish view on\par local bonds," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2  analyst Roxana Hulea said in a\par note dated Jan 14.\par     "Abating import demand and (expected) official approval of\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 SBA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (an \f28 \uc2 \f2 IMF\f28 \uc2 \f2  credit line) will likely give way to the\par stabilisation of the dinar and the resumption of the easing\par cycle," she added.\par     The Czech crown eased 0.1 percent to the euro to\par 28.104.\par     Czech President Milos Zeman talked the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  up on\par Wednesday, saying the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should halt its policy of\par keeping the crown weak through a pledge to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. \par     "While Hungary and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  still have room to manoeuvre with\par their interest rates, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would have to opt\par for a new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regime border (currently at EUR/CZK 27),"\par Raiffeisen said in a note.\par     "Whereas we project high probability of more short-term\par pressure on CZK, we would currently not expect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to adjust the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regime border higher," it added.    \par  *                                                            *\par  **************** CEE MARKETS SNAPSHOT AT 0953 CET ************ \par  ************************* \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  *************************\par                             Latest  Previous   Daily   Change  \par                             bid     close      change  in 2015 \par  Czech crown                 28.104    28.065   -0.14%  -1.61% \par  Hungary forint             318.900   319.765   +0.27%  -0.76% \par  Polish zloty                 4.257     4.259   +0.04%  +0.66% \par  Romanian leu                 4.492     4.496   +0.08%  -0.25% \par  Croatian kuna                7.687     7.684   -0.04%  -0.42% \par  Serbian dinar              122.470   122.600   +0.11%  -0.91% \par  Note: daily change calculated from previous close at 1800 CET \par  **************************** STOCKS **************************\par                             Latest   Previous  Daily   Change  \par                                      close     change  in 2015 \par  Prague                       958.85   958.80   +0.01%  +0.76% \par  Budapest                   16099.00 16066.13   +0.20%  -2.54% \par  Warsaw                      2341.00  2336.66   +0.19%  +0.77% \par  Bucharest                   7010.85  7014.14   -0.05%  +1.61% \par  Ljubljana                    777.55   779.54   -0.26%  -0.26% \par  Zagreb                      1789.77  1787.94   +0.10%  +2.85% \par  Sofia                        495.43   494.49   +0.19%  -5.42% \par  ***************************** BONDS **************************\par                         Yield    Yield    Spread     Daily     \par                         (bid)    change   vs Bund    change in \par  Czech Republic                                      spread  