\par\par \b \uc2 Czech Republic - Factors To Watch on Jan 15\b0\par\par\uc2 596 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 2015\par 08:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PRAGUE, Jan 15 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press\par reports and events to watch which may affect Czech financial\par markets on Thursday. \par        \par     ALL TIMES GMT (Czech Republic: GMT + 1 hours)         \par =========================ECONOMIC DATA========================\par     Real-time economic data releases................... \par     Previous stories on Czech data............ \par     Overview of economic data and forecasts......... \par     Updates on CEE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ........................... \par ===========================EVENTS==============================\par     PRAGUE - \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governing board to hold a\par regular weekly meeting. It is not scheduled to discuss monetary\par policy issues.\par     Related news:       \par ===========================NEWS================================ \par   \par     C.BANK: The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should halt its policy of\par keeping the crown weak through a pledge to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, President Milos Zeman said on Wednesday.\par     The crown gained 0.7 percent to 28.053 to the euro\par , reversing the day's losses after the comments.\par     Zeman has no power over the independent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par decisions but he spoke at a sensitive time when the market has\par been speculating whether then \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may need to weaken\par the crown further by fresh \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to bring inflation up.\par     Story: Related news: \par     \par     POLISH ENERGY: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is considering merging its four major\par power producers into two companies strong enough to compete with\par larger European rivals and possibly support the country's\par flagging coal industry, two market sources told Reuters on\par Wednesday.\par     The two new companies would have the financial heft to make\par the investments needed to compete with rival companies across\par Europe such as Czech CEZ, central Europe's biggest\par utility.\par     Story: Related news: \par     \par     NWR: Czech coal miner New World Resources' \par  produced 2.269 million tonnes of coking coal in the\par last quarter of 2014, bringing its annual output to 8.601\par million tonnes, just below its target range.\par     Story: Related news: \par     \par     CEE MARKETS: Central European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regained some\par ground on Wednesday after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would\par not rush into rate cuts and the Czech president talked up the\par crown.\par     Story: Related news: \par \par     CEE POWER: Forecasts for a steep rise in wind generation in\par the region pushed central and southeastern European day ahead\par power prices lower on Wednesday, with Romanian and Hungarian\par spot prices retaining their strong premium, traders said.\par     Story: Related news: \par  ---------------------- MARKET SNAPSHOT ------------------------\par  Index/Crown \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest     Prev   Pct change Pct change\par                                     close    on day     in 2015\par  vs Euro        28.025     28.198    0.61      -1.35\par  vs Dollar         23.811     23.838    0.11      -4.29\par  Czech Equities    958.8      958.8     -0.46       1.28\par  U.S. Equities 17,427.09  17,613.68    -1.06      -2.22\par  Pvs close or current levels vs prior domestic close at 1600 GMT\par ======================PRESS DIGEST============================\par     BETTING: The Finance Ministry is looking at plans to be able\par to tax foreign online betting groups operating in the country. A\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Betfair\f28 \uc2 \f2  representative said the plan could lead to the exit of\par big players from the market.\par     Hospdarske Noviny, page 1\par         \par     Reuters has not verified the media reports, nor does it \par vouch for their accuracy.\par    \par  For Instant Views of key economic data click on \par  For summary of economic data and forecasts     \par  For diary of forthcoming Czech events          \par  For calendar of east European economic indicators  \par  TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets                   \par  TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch                  \par  \par  For an economic indicator diary for the euro zone, the United \par  States and other Group of Seven countries see \par  \par  For real-time stock market index quotes click in brackets: \par  Warsaw WIG20  Budapest BUX Prague PX \par  \par     News editor of the day: Jan Lopatka on +420 224 190 474\par     E-mail: prague.newsroom@thomsonreuters.com\par \par  (Reporting by Prague Newsroom)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-1-15T08:13:54.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150115eb1f007cc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
