\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Emerging-market assets get respite as dollar pulls back\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sujata Rao   \par \uc2 732 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 2014\par 11:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Oct 9 (Reuters) - A decline by the dollar boosted most emerging-market assets on Thursday, with the main equity index up 1 percent and bond yields at multi-week or even record lows. The rouble steadied after hefty \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Bond yields in \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit record lows across the curve after a larger-than-expected rate cut, dragging down yields in central Europe. South African yields tumbled to one-month lows, tracking \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  moves.\par \par \uc2 The dollar and U.S. bond yields fell after minutes of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's last meeting suggested the \uc2 Fed\uc2  would maintain its accommodative monetary policy. Traders said some expectations for the \uc2 Fed\uc2 's first rate rise have shifted to September 2015 from June.\par \par \uc2 "Dollar weakness, EM happy!" said \uc2 Ilan Solot\uc2 , a strategist at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 . "I personally think this is an opportunity to go long dollar again. It's obvious this is a temporary pullback for the dollar."\par \par \uc2 MSCI's emerging equity index rose 1.2 percent . Russian stocks jumped almost 2 percent, getting help from slightly higher oil prices . Bourses in central Europe rose 1 to 2 percent .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Malaysian ringgit to the South African rand rose from multi-week lows against the dollar. The rand gained 0.3 percent, rising for the fourth straight day. South African bond yields meanwhile fell to one-month lows, having declined more than 30 basis points this week.\par \par \uc2 But the mood towards Russia remained bearish. Western sanctions and corporate demand for dollars to repay external debt have pushed the rouble to record lows and kept foreigners out of local stock and bond markets.\par \par \uc2 Ten-year rouble bond yields were at three-week highs and the rouble held near the psychologically key level of 40 per dollar , even though by some estimates the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold around $3.5 billion from Friday to Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The bank moved the rouble trading band against a euro-dollar basket by 20 kopecks on Wednesday, implying heavy dollar sales.\par \par \uc2 Benoit Anne, head of emerging markets strategy at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  said Russia needed to change its tactics on the rouble.\par \par \uc2 "This piecemeal, soft \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is simply a waste of reserves. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is too gentle to influence the market ... which means that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is set to burn $1 billion a day or so in official reserves for the foreseeable future," Anne said in a note.\par \par \uc2 "I would rather see a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that would engage in much more powerful action ... In fact, I would prefer to see an interest-rate defense of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept rates on hold last month but hinted it might raise them if its inflation target was in danger.\par \par \uc2 Central European bonds extended gains after Poland cut rates by a 50 bps, more than expected. Polish yields tumbled to record lows across the curve, with 10-year yields now at 2.75 percent , down 20 bps from their Monday close.\par \par \uc2 Hungarian yields also fell to record lows, with the 10-year down 25 bps to 4.15 percent.\par \par \uc2 Citi analysts advised buying 10-year Polish and Hungarian bonds, noting the trade also benefits from euro zone stimulus.\par \par \uc2 "We are getting back to central European bonds, we are buying (zloty and forint) unhedged," they told clients.\par \par \uc2 The Turkish lira rose to two-week highs after the \uc2 Fed\uc2  message. Ten-year bond yields fell around 15 bps. Stocks rose 2.5 percent to one-week highs\par \par \uc2 Analysts advise caution on Turkish assets because of fighting in Syria. At least 21 people were killed on Wednesday after Turkish Kurds protested against the government for doing nothing to protect Kurds in Syria.\par \par \uc2 "Given the confluence of negative political and economic developments, Turkish assets should underperform," Solot of BBH said.\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  performance 2014, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jus35t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jus35t}}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on MSCI emerging index performance 2014, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/weh36s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/weh36s}}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on MSCI emerging Europe performance 2014, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jun28s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jun28s}}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on MSCI frontier index performance 2014, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/zyh97s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/zyh97s}}}\par \par \uc2 For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par \uc2 For TURKISH market report, see\par \par \uc2 For RUSSIAN market report, see ) (Additional reporting by Chris Vellacott; Editing by Larry King) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-10-9T10:39:46.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141009eaa900a1f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
