\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2  c.bank governor say may  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  if zloty too volatile\b0\par\par\uc2 145 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 2014\par 16:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, June 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Marek Belka said on Tuesday the bank has the option of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if it believes the zloty is too volatile.\par \par \uc2 The Polish zloty gained more than one percent versus euro in the last two weeks on speculation that the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may cut rates, increasing the credit cost disparity between Poland and euro zone.\par \par \uc2 "We are here adhering to a policy of a free-float for the zloty, supplemented with the possibility of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when we recognize that market dynamics are extensive," Belka told a news conference when asked if he was worried about the strength of the zloty. (Reporting by Karolina Slowikowska; Writing by Marcin Goclowski; Editing by Christian Lowe) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-6-3T15:41:57.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140603ea63006qq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
