\par\par \b \uc2 *Belka: We're Not Ruling Out Changing Polish Rates in '14\b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 2014\par 16:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 3 Jun 2014 10:08 ET *Belka: Polish 1Q GDP at 3.4%/Year Very Good, Economy Accelerates\par \par \uc2 3 Jun 2014 10:08 ET *Belka: Polish CPI Very Low and Likely to Stay That Way\par \par \uc2 3 Jun 2014 10:08 ET *Belka: Polish GDP, CPI Are Factors Working in Opposite Directions\par \par \uc2 3 Jun 2014 10:09 ET *Belka: Declines to Comment on Possible Direction of Next Poland Rates Move\par \par \uc2 3 Jun 2014 10:09 ET *Belka: Polish Economy is Accelerating, Monetary Policy Shouldn't Be Pro-Cyclical\par \par \uc2 3 Jun 2014 10:09 ET *Belka: But Polish CPI Is Surprisingly Low\par \par \uc2 3 Jun 2014 10:11 ET *Belka: Polish CPI May Be Negative In Some Months of This Year\par \par \uc2 3 Jun 2014 10:12 ET *Belka: We're Not Planning, But Not Ruling Out Poland Rate Cut\par \par \uc2 3 Jun 2014 10:13 ET *Belka: With Low CPI, Real Polish Interest Rate Is Higher\par \par \uc2 3 Jun 2014 10:13 ET *Belka: Poland Rate Cut Not Base Scenario\par \par \uc2 3 Jun 2014 10:22 ET *Belka: 'I Wouldn't Rule Out Poland Rate Cuts or A Rate Cut'\par \par \uc2 3 Jun 2014 10:24 ET *Belka: Much of Low Polish CPI Is Imported, It Doesn't Complicate Recovery\par \par \uc2 3 Jun 2014 10:30 ET *Belka: \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  Runs Free-Floating \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Policy With Possibilities of \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 3 Jun 2014 10:30 ET *\uc2 National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  Ends Press Conference After Rate Decision\par \par \uc2 3 Jun 2014 11:00 ET  Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Returns to Rate Cut Talk as CPI Very Low\par \par \uc2 By Marcin Sobczyk\par \par \uc2 WARSAW--Polish interest rates could be cut because consumer price growth is very low and may turn into deflation later this year, National Bank of Poland Governor Marek Belka said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Belka left the possibility of a rate cut open after inflation fell to 0.3% on the year in April. The bank had promised to keep rates unchanged "at least" until the end of the third quarter of this year, but on Tuesday it deleted "at least" from its monthly statement.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will offer new guidance in July but rates may change this year still, Mr. Belka said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Belka said the Polish economy is accelerating, with growth 3.4% on the year in the first quarter, a factor that would support tighter policy. But very low CPI is a factor working in the opposite direction, he added.\par \par \uc2 Write to Marcin Sobczyk at marcin.sobczyk@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 03, 2014 11:00 ET (15:00 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140603ea63002bj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
