\par\par \b \uc2 *Polish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Chief Marek Belka Speaks in Warsaw\b0\par\par\uc2 434 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 16:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 5 Mar 2014 10:25 EDT *NBP Belka: We're Not Talking About Raising Rates in Poland\par \par \uc2 5 Mar 2014 10:26 EDT *NBP Belka: Polish CPI Projected to Near 2.5% by 2016\par \par \uc2 5 Mar 2014 10:27 EDT *NBP Belka: Another Polish Rate Cut Would Be Strange, Pro-Cyclical\par \par \uc2 5 Mar 2014 10:28 EDT *NBP Belka: Polish Rates Policy Also Needs to Watch Market Stability\par \par \uc2 5 Mar 2014 10:28 EDT *NBP Belka: Poland Not Facing Asset Bubbles, But We Need Vigilance\par \par \uc2 5 Mar 2014 10:38 EDT *NBP Belka: Window for Polish Rate Hikes Always Exists, But No Promise\par \par \uc2 5 Mar 2014 10:38 EDT *NBP Belka: No Promise of Polish Rate Hikes After 3Q\par \par \uc2 5 Mar 2014 10:39 EDT *NBP Belka: Stresses Polish Rates Should Remain Unchanged for Longer\par \par \uc2 5 Mar 2014 10:45 EDT *\uc2 National Bank of Poland\uc2  Ends Conference after Rate Decision\par \par \uc2 5 Mar 2014 11:26 EDT  Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Keeps Benchmark Rate Unchanged\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By Marcin Sobczyk \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WARSAW-\f28 \uc2 \f2 Poland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday extended its informal neutral bias faced with subdued price growth, a moderate economic recovery and the Russian-Ukrainian conflict, the bank's governor said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The bank left the benchmark rate unchanged at 2.5%, the lowest on record, and said borrowing costs would remain unchanged until at least the end of the third quarter of this year and possibly even longer. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Poland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  previously said rates would remain on hold until at least the end of the second quarter.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Poland should have very low consumer price inflation for longer than previously expected, said Marek Belka, head of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Poland's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The bank said CPI would likely be near the 2.5% target some time in 2016.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Russian-Ukrainian conflict and what \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sees as an armed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Crimea accelerated the extension of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's neutral stance on rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The situation in Ukraine sped up our decision to show that we don't see any threats for the economy, at least as to monetary policy," Mr. Belka said. "We wanted to show our confidence in the strength of the economy's fundamentals and the zloty."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  briefly reacted to heightened tensions between Russia and Ukraine this week, moving near 4.22 zlotys to the euro on Monday. On Wednesday afternoon, it was back near 4.18, stable on the day.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Marcin Sobczyk at marcin.sobczyk@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 05, 2014 11:26 ET (16:26 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140305ea35002tv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
