\par\par \b \uc2 Polish PM Says No Need to  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  to Prop Up Zloty - Report\b0\par\par\uc2 362 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2014\par 10:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW--\b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the zloty hit by a broader emerging-markets selloff, the country's prime minister said over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 The Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has weakened some 2.5% to the euro since mid-January, trading near 4.25 on Monday morning.\par \par \uc2 "When we compare the situation of the zloty with [the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of] other emerging markets, the weakening is luckily incomparably smaller than is the case with other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whether it's the forint, the Turkish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Indian rupee, or \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Argentina or Brazil," Donald Tusk said, according to state newswire PAP.\par \par \uc2 "We have institutions that have various tools and instruments to act in situations that require such action. At this point, fortunately there's no such need, but we're watching this very closely," he said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , independent from the government, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2011 and again in June 2013 to prop up the zloty when it was weakening rapidly. In 2013, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  occurred with the zloty above 4.30 to the euro. In 2011, they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the zloty around 4.50 to the euro.\par \par \uc2 The government has the ability to buy zlotys in the market with the euros and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at its disposal. At the end of December, the \uc2 Polish finance ministry\uc2  held an equivalent of 3.16 billion euro ($4.26 billion). It can also buy \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the state-owned bank BGK.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Tusk said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this time may not be effective because the zloty is weakening due to global factors.\par \par \uc2 "If we recognized the zloty was a victim of speculation, of any action focused on our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  more than once in a rapid and effective way," he said. "If the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is exposed to global events, \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  bear risk and may not be effective. In any case, there's no reason for any non-standard reaction for now."\par \par \uc2 Agency website: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.pap.pl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.pap.pl}}}\par \par \uc2 Write to Marcin Sobczyk at marcin.sobczyk@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 03, 2014 04:04 ET (09:04 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140203ea23000s5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
