\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Polish PM Tusk sees no need to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  to support zloty\b0\par\par\uc2 258 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2014\par 12:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds background)\par \par \uc2 WARSAW, Feb 1 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Prime Minister \uc2 Donald Tusk\uc2  said on Saturday he saw no need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the zloty as its recent weakening is related to global risk-aversion and is insignificant compared with other emerging markets' \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "If the zloty follows the global mood, then \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are ineffective. There is no need for a reaction," Tusk told a news conference.\par \par \uc2 "When we compare the zloty situation to other emerging markets it is obvious that the zloty's weakening is thankfully much smaller that what is going on with other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to a five-month low on Friday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the zloty last June when it traded at about 4.3 zlotys to the euro, and the bank has repeatedly said it is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb excessive volatility. At 1057 GMT on Saturday zloty was trading at 4.2375 versus euro.\par \par \uc2 Poland's is seen as one of the most resilient economies in the region, but the zloty has been hit by the global sell-off in emerging assets.\par \par \uc2 The former communist country has posted nearly two decades of uninterrupted growth but its economy slowed sharply last year and growth fell to near zero in the first quarter of 2013. It has been gathering pace since then. ($1 = 3.1523 Polish zlotys) (Reporting by Marcin Goclowski; Editing by Hugh Lawson)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-2-4T11:15:50.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140201ea210076d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
