\par\par \b \uc2 CEE Morning Briefing: US Budget Deal Overshadows Local Events\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sean Carney   \par \uc2 664 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Oktober 2013\par 04:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \par Local/GMT \par 1130/0930 Hungary government bond auction \par 1400/1200 Polish Sep Indus Output, PPI, \par           \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  minutes \par N/A       IMF delegation visits Slovenia \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market sentiment in central Europe will be driven Thursday by the United States' budget and debt deal, with the result likely to affect already volatile \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were turbulent Wednesday, with the Czech koruna weakening sharply on speculation of a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's zloty and the Hungarian forint both weakened and later firmed on hopes that the U.S. budget impasse would be overcome.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  is starting a fact-finding mission in Slovenia, the euro-zone country considered to be the next potential candidate for a sovereign bailout due to its heavily indebted, state-run banks.\par \par \uc2 The IMF delegation will review proposed budget drafts for 2014 and 2015 and evaluate the Slovenian cabinet's progress on the clean-up of its three major state-owned banks. The visit comes ahead of the launch of the country's bad bank next month that is hoped will resolve the bad loans weighing on Slovenia's banking sector.\par \par \uc2 In Warsaw, Poland's statistics office will release September industrial output data that analysts said should confirm a minor acceleration in economic growth.\par \par \uc2 In Hungary, the government will auction three-, five- and ten-year government bonds and seeks to raise 43 billion forints ($197.3 million). \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par EUR/CZK \par Latest 0150 GMT 25.666-99 \par Previous 2150 GMT 25.656-708 \par %Chg +0.00 \par  \par EUR/HUF \par Latest 0150 GMT 294.61-5.48 \par Previous 2150 GMT 294.60-5.24 \par % Chg  +0.04 \par  \par EUR/PLN \par Latest 0150 GMT 4.1631-84 \par Previous 2150 GMT 4.1617-78 \par % Chg  +0.02 \par  \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par Hungary \par          Wed    Tue \par 3 yrs    4.39%  4.42% \par 5 yrs    4.88%  4.90% \par 10yrs    5.62%  5.63% \par  \par Poland \par          Wed    Tue \par 3 yrs    3.06%  3.07%(1) \par 5 yrs    3.60%  3.58% \par 10yrs    4.33%  4.31% \par (1) 2 yrs \par  \par Czech Republic \par          Wed    Tue \par 3 yrs    0.38%  0.38% \par 5 yrs    1.16%  1.16% \par 10yrs    2.40%  2.40%(1) \par (1) 11 yrs \par  \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG 20 \par 2,505.20+14.86+0.60% \par  \par BUX \par 18,420.61-292.93-1.57% \par  \par PX \par 981.77+5.51+0.56% \par  \par OTHER NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Poland's interest rates could stay on hold for the next year as there is no risk of inflation accelerating amid a sluggish economic recovery, monetary policy council member Jan Winiecki told TOK FM radio Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Winiecki, who opposed the latest interest rate cuts when the 10-strong rate panel brought the borrowing costs to a record low of 2.5%, is also skeptical the U.S. Federal Reserve will back out of its easy-money policies soon.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Mario Draghi has asked the Hungarian government to provide information about its plans to resolve the problems facing foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  loan holders, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hungarian Economy Ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  told the Wall Street Journal Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ministry said it replied in a letter to Mr. Draghi, but didn't reveal details of its response.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The recipient should decide about the publication of the content of the letter," the ministry said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: Romanian new passenger car sales fell 9.8% on the year to 43,324 units in the January-September period, the Automotive Manufacturers and Importers Association, or APIA, said Wednesday, news agency Mediafax reports.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Veronika Gulyas in Budapest, Patryk Wasilewski in Warsaw and Leos Rousek in Prague contributed to this article.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Sean Carney at sean.carney@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/}}}\uc2 \f2  for the WSJ blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 16, 2013 22:12 ET (02:12 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131017e9ah000eb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
