\par\par \b \uc2 DJ South African Rand Leads Gains Among Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Prabha Natarajan   \par \uc2 439 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 2013\par 18:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The South African rand recovered and led a strengthening of most emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell 0.87% against the rand, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 As the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  shutdown heads into its second day, market participants are uncertain as to how long the impasse in congressional negotiations would last. Some investors have scaled back from long dollar positions, and added exposure, at least temporarily to emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Our view is that this is a dollar negative," said Lauren van Biljon, strategist at First Advantage Wells Fargo International bond fund.\par \par \uc2 In her firm, they have added exposure to the Polish zloty but scaled back some of the exposure to the Mexican peso last week. But, for the most part, she said they were waiting for more clarity before stepping back into the market.\par \par \uc2 "It's just stunned silence now," she said. "Nothing is happening, so we can't trade on it."\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso has lagged other emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past two days as investors take into account Mexico's close ties to the U.S. and on worries that if the U.S. economy were to slow down once again, Mexico would be affected too.\par \par \uc2 The short-term outlook on Mexico also has weakened as the country's growth rate is expected slow down below 1.5% this year under the double whammy of hurricanes Ingrid and Manuel.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fetched MXN13.1478 on the day, a tad better than the MXN13.1543 close the previous day.\par \par \uc2 The rand benefited from the improved sentiment among investors.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had trailed in recent sessions on global factors and concerns about local mining strikes, was once again edging closer to ZAR10 to the dollar, a critical level. Earlier in the day, the dollar-rand pair had soared to ZAR10.1526 for the first time in a week.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, the Brazilian real has come back on the expectations of more rate increases, a policy with a focus on bringing more investment dollars into the country and a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at its meeting left its key policy rates unchanged and said it didn't expect to be affected by the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  shutdown or debt-ceiling negotiations.\par \par \uc2 The euro traded at PLN4.2142, a slightly weaker on the day, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 Write to Prabha Natarajan at prabha.natarajan@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 02, 2013 12:37 ET (16:37 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131002e9a20045l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
