\par\par \b \uc2 Polish  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Chief Belka: We Don't Like Rapid  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Moves\b0\par\par\uc2 142 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2013\par 10:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW--The \uc2 National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  stands ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the zloty market in case of any rapid moves caused by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation, said Marek Belka, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor.\par \par \uc2 He said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are "sporadic" and not designed to defend any specific exchangel level of the zloty.\par \par \uc2 "We don't like rapid exchange-rate moves," he said on business news channel TVN CNBC, adding such rapid swings in the value of the zloty against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  destabilizes the economy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on June 7 pushing the zloty to PLN4.24 to the euro that day from PLN4.30 a day earlier. At 0828 GMT Friday, the zloty traded at PLN4.22.\par \par \uc2 Write to Marcin Sobczyk at marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com [ 26-07-13 0830GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130726e97q000ez\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
