\par\par \b \uc2 INSTANT VIEW 2-Polish C/A swings to highest surplus in at least 13 years\b0\par\par\uc2 444 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 2013\par 14:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW, June 17 (Reuters) - Poland's current account swung in April to its highest surplus on the record spanning back 13 years, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Monday. The surplus of 468 million euro ($624.31 million), boosted by a rise in exports, contrasted with analysts' expectations of a 185 million deficit. Poland's exports rose by 12.3 percent year-on-year, data show, pointing to an improvement in the country's main export market, Germany. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     FORECAST:\par     Analysts polled by Reuters expected a current account\par deficit of 185 million euro. \par     \par     MARKET REACTION\par     The Polish zloty was little changed immediately\par after the data.\par          \par     ANALYSTS' COMMENTS:\par     PETER ATTARD MONTALTO, ECONOMIST AT NOMURA: \par     "This record bumping monthly C/A number was partly due to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 transfer timing issues but underneath there is strenght in services, which is an ongoing trend, but the weakness in domestic demand versus an export sector that continues to do O.K. is the key story looking through the monthly volatility. "It shows however that PLN is a 'safe' \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  given its smaller \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  account deficit than some other EM peers."\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     \par     JAROSLAW JANECKI, ECONOMIST AT \f28 \uc2 \f2 SOCIETE GENERALE\f28 \uc2 \f2  IN WARSAW:\par     "The data proves that trade is strong and has significantly\par contributed to economic growth. The highest ever surplus is \par mainly a result of a higher export growth. \par     "In the short term the data may support the Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par It is rather neutral for the Monetary Policy Council." \par     \par     PIOTR BIELSKI, SENIOR ECONOMIST AT BZ WBK:\par     "The figures are double positive. First, they indicate a\par surplus and second is the source. We saw a great reading in\par exports, they rose by 12 percent.\par     "It's too early to say whther this reverses the trend.\par Perhaps there were some one-off factors.\par     "These figures improve our view of the economic outlook. We\par now expect that the rise in GDP in the second quarter will be\par higher than we earlier thought.\par     "These numbers should have a positive impact on the zloty. I\par don't think they will be a deciding factor for the MPC. The\par Council keeps an eye on inflation which will be near zero in the\par coming months."    \par     \par     BACKGROUND:\par     * Polish cbank says Finance Ministry interfering\par  \par     * Polish central banker Glapinski opposed to more rate cuts\par  \par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to bolster zloty \par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cuts rates to new low, sees limited room for more\par easing \par     * Polish PMI improves slightly in May to 48 points\par  \par     * Polish economy set to improve in Q2 - finance ministry\par    \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ($1 = 0.7496 euros) (Compiled by Marcin Goettig)\f28 \par \par \uc2 POLAND-INFLATION/ (INSTANT VIEW 2) | ABN | M | PX | D | E | RBN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130620e96h000ob\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
