ress the concerns of companies exploring for shale gas in the central European country in a bid to speed up growth of the fledging industry.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The proposed "geological and mining law," which has been nearly two years in the making, has now been sent to the prime minister's chancellery to await a government meeting at which it can be approved or discussed further.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Audi AG\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the premium brand of German car maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen AG\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Wednesday opened the latest expansion of its car manufacturing plant in Gyor, Hungary, where it is launching the mass production of its model A3 Limousine.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The development will allow the firm to manufacture up to 500 model A3 Limousines a day, or some 125,000 cars a year, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Audi\f28 \uc2 \f2  executives said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Veronika Gulyas in Budapest and Marynia Kruk in Warsaw contributed to this article.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Sean Carney at sean.carney@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/}}}\uc2 \f2  for the WSJ blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region. [ 13-06-13 0156GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020130613e96d00001\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
