\par\par \b \uc2 DJ CEE MORNING BRIEFING: Hungary Debt Sale Eyed as Yields Rising\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sean Carney   \par \uc2 707 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2013\par 03:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \par Local/GMT \par 1130/0930 Hungary government bond auction \par 1400/1200 Polish May inflation \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rising bond yields on markets across Europe are making Thursday's debt sale in Budapest an event to watch, while in Poland fresh inflation data may put the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in a pickle.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Hungary's Government Debt Management Agency\uc2  plans to sell a total of 38 billion forints ($169.5 million) worth of bonds at auction, which comes as the country's sovereign yields have risen around 150 basis points over the past two weeks.\par \par \uc2 Amid global concerns that the U.S. Federal Reserve and other central banks may wind down their easy money policies, investors have reduced exposure to regional bond markets, pushing yields higher and making \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatile.\par \par \uc2 Dalimil Vyskovsky, a fixed-income trader at \uc2 Komercni Banka\uc2  in Prague, said that rising yields create a good buying opportunity.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the \uc2 Czech Finance Ministry\uc2  auctioned two bond issues. Demand for a 15-year paper was subdued, but the six-year paper was nearly twice oversubscribed, indicating that cash-rich local banks are eager to invest in higher yielding assets, Mr. Vyskovsky said.\par \par \uc2 In Warsaw, Poland's consumer inflation is expected to edge down further, putting the country's Monetary Policy Council in a bind about whether to further cut interest rates in July to stimulate economic growth, but risking additional zloty sell-offs.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Friday, pushing the zloty to about 4.22 against the euro from 4.30 earlier that week. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have said their intention is not to fight a trend, but to curtail speculator-driven volatility. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par EUR/CZK \par Latest 0150 GMT 25.554-97 \par Previous 2150 GMT 25.535-94 \par %Chg +0.04 \par  \par EUR/HUF \par Latest 0150 GMT 296.43-92 \par Previous 2150 GMT 296.35-07 \par % Chg  -0.02 \par  \par EUR/PLN \par Latest 0150 GMT 4.2567-674 \par Previous 2150 GMT 4.2520-700 \par % Chg  +0.03 \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par Hungary \par         Wed    Tues \par 3 yrs   5.10%  5.20% \par 5 yrs   5.65%  5.75% \par 10yrs   6.10%  6.30% \par  \par Poland \par         Wed    Tues \par 3 yrs   2.82%  2.90%(1) \par 5 yrs   3.39%  3.47% \par 10yrs   3.90%  3.96% \par (1) 2 yrs \par  \par Czech Republic \par         Wed    Tues \par 3 yrs   0.48%  0.48% \par 5 yrs   1.41%  1.52% \par 10yrs   2.23%  2.24%(1) \par (1) 11 yrs \par  \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG 20 \par 2,481.60 -2.51 -0.10% \par  \par BUX \par 19,542.72 -46.83 -0.24% \par  \par PX \par 934.76 -8.67 -0.92% \par  \par OTHER NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: \f28 \uc2 \f2 PKO Bank Polski\f28 \uc2 \f2  SA (PKO.WA), Poland's largest lender by assets, bought the local unit of Scandinavian bank \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nordea Bank AB\f28 \uc2 \f2  (NRBAY, NDA.SK, NDA1V.HE) for 2.83 billion zlotys ($890 million), the banks said late Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PKO BP bought shares in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nordea Bank Polska\f28 \uc2 \f2  bank as well as life insurance company Nordea Polska Life and Nordea Finance Polska.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Poland's environment ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  has amended its proposed hydrocarbon law to address the concerns of companies exploring for shale gas in the central European country in a bid to speed up growth of the fledging industry.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The proposed "geological and mining law," which has been nearly two years in the making, has now been sent to the prime minister's chancellery to await a government meeting at which it can be approved or discussed further.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Audi AG\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the premium brand of German car maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen AG\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Wednesday opened the latest expansion of its car manufacturing plant in Gyor, Hungary, where it is launching the mass production of its model A3 Limousine.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The development will allow the firm to manufacture up to 500 model A3 Limousines a day, or some 125,000 cars a year, Audi executives said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Veronika Gulyas in Budapest and Marynia Kruk in Warsaw contributed to this article.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Sean Carney at sean.carney@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/}}}\uc2 \f2  for the WSJ blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 12, 2013 21:56 ET (01:56 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130613e96d0005c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
