\par\par \b \uc2 CEE MORNING BRIEFING: Hungarian CPI to Accelerate but Still Low\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sean Carney   \par \uc2 574 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2013\par 04:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TODAY'S CALENDAR \par Local/GMT \par 0900/0700 Hungary May CPI \par 1100/0900 \f28 \uc2 \f2 PKN Orlen\f28 \uc2 \f2  Czech unit Unipetrol briefing on strategy \par 1130/0930 Hungary 3-month T-bill auction \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Accelerating Hungarian inflation should remain well-below targeted levels Tuesday, supporting calls for looser monetary policy, while in Prague, the country's largest refiner will announce its new business strategy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 Hungary's headline inflation is widely expected to have accelerated to 1.9% on the year in May from 1.7% in April, according to economists polled by The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 That forecast rate of inflation is comfortably below the \uc2 Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 3% medium-term target, giving the bank's rate-setters room to again ease monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut its base rate by 25 basis points from 4.5% to a fresh record low of 4.25% later this month.\par \par \uc2 In Prague, \uc2 Unipetrol AS\uc2  (BAAUNIPE.PR), majority-owned by Poland's \uc2 PKN Orlen SA\uc2  (PKN.WA), will hold a press briefing to outline its new business strategy through 2017.\par \par \uc2 Unipetrol\uc2 , which also operates retail filling stations and petrochemical \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has only intermittently generated a profit recently due to low margins, high logistics costs and a rampant local black market for motor fuels.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par  \par EUR/CZK \par Latest 0150 GMT 25.688-744 \par Previous 2150 GMT 25.688-753 \par %Chg -0.02 \par  \par EUR/HUF \par Latest 0150 GMT 298.65-9.42 \par Previous 2150 GMT 298.87-9.52 \par % Chg -0.05 \par  \par EUR/PLN \par Latest 0150 GMT 4.2696-754 \par Previous 2150 GMT 4.2657-739 \par % Chg +0.06 \par  \par FIXED INCOME \par  \par Hungary \par         Mon    Fri \par 3 yrs   4.99%  4.75% \par 5 yrs   5.45%  5.30% \par 10yrs   5.99%  5.85% \par  \par Poland \par         Mon    Fri \par 3 yrs   2.90%  2.83%(1) \par 5 yrs   3.40%  3.26% \par 10yrs   3.87%  3.73% \par (1) 2 yrs \par  \par Czech Republic \par         Mon    Fri \par 3 yrs   0.49%  0.50% \par 5 yrs   1.18%  1.25% \par 10yrs   2.18%  2.07%(1) \par (1) 11 yrs \par  \par STOCKS \par  \par WIG 20 \par 2,503.41    +14.57   +0.59% \par  \par BUX \par 19,743.65  +111.02   +0.57% \par  \par PX \par 949.78       -7.67   -0.80% \par  \par  \par OTHER NEWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 POLAND: Poland's public finance debt rose 3.5% to 869.9 billion zlotys ($270 billion) in the first three months of the year as the government had to take on more debt to finance this year's budget deficit, the finance ministry said Monday.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 POLAND\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Polish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in markets to strengthen the zloty following its surprise move to bolster the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Friday, but it could find itself swimming against a very powerful tide of emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakness, analysts said Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Hungarian car parts and vehicle manufacturer Raba Jarmu Kft. and Renault Trucks Defense signed a letter of intent Monday to jointly manufacture undercarriages for fire trucks, the Hungarian firm said. Raba Jarmu is a unit of partly-state owned Raba Jarmuipari Holding Nyrt. (RABA.BU), and Renault Trucks Defense is wholly owned by Renault Trucks, part of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volvo AB (VOLVY)\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Sean Carney at sean.carney@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope/}}}\uc2 \f2  for the WSJ blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region. [ 11-06-13 0221GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1806 75091   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130611e96b00025\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
