\par\par \b \uc2 Poland May Struggle to Support the Zloty\b0\par\par\uc2 By Patryk Wasilewski and Clare Connaghan   \par \uc2 746 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2013\par 17:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WARSAW--The \uc2 Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets to strengthen the zloty following its surprise move to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday, but it could find itself swimming against a very powerful tide of emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness, analysts said Monday.\par \par \uc2 Market watchers believe the bank sold some 200 million euros ($264 million) Friday, pushing the zloty to about PLN4.22 from above PLN4.30, after it weakened sharply earlier in the week.\par \par \uc2 Many saw it as a pre-emptive move to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the likely negative impact of the U.S. Federal Reserve phasing out its quantitative easing plan.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a history of using \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help achieve its economic goals. In 2011, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the finance ministry repeatedly sold foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in exchange for the zloty. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wanted to clamp down on unruly market behavior while the finance ministry aimed to keep Poland's foreign debt below levels that would trigger austerity measures under the country's self-imposed system of debt thresholds.\par \par \uc2 It may not be so straightforward this time. Some analysts warn that \uc2 Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't have enough foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firepower to prop up the zloty if there is a strong a downward trend across the emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The big difference is that in 2011 we had local factors at play and local goals," said BZ WBK economist Piotr Bielski.\par \par \uc2 This time the zloty is coming under pressure alongside all emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bonds following the U.S. Federal Reserve's recent comment that it could soon start winding down its bond-buying program.\par \par \uc2 The prospect of tighter U.S. monetary policy has prompted many investors to sell riskier assets in favor of safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bonds.\par \par \uc2 A Warsaw-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said that if the U.S. were to unwind QE quickly, the \uc2 Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be left struggling if it tries to bet against the market. "It could be able to smooth the ride or slow it down at most," the dealer said.\par \par \uc2 In 2011 the \uc2 Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  worth much less than EUR5 billion, governor Marek Belka said at the time. In May the bank's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at EUR84.7 billion.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems aware it is unlikely to buck the global trend and wants instead to show that investors who speculate against the zloty will be punished.\par \par \uc2 "Somebody thought he will make money on the zloty's weakening and got burned," Mr. Belka said after Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ING BSK's chief Warsaw economist, Rafal Benecki, suggested investors should heed the governor's words if they are looking for clues about future \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Instead of looking at how close the zloty is to PLN4.3 against the euro they should monitor the speed of any changes and the broader regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trend.\par \par \uc2 "The zloty was weakening faster than other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region and this is what most likely worried the NBP," said ING's Mr. Benecki.\par \par \uc2 The zloty fell 0.75% against the euro on Monday, slightly less than the Hungarian forint and slightly more than the Czech koruna.\par \par \uc2 Still, the \uc2 Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't scare everyone.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  really doesn't change my view. The Polish zloty remains a sell," said Benoit Anne, head of emerging market strategy at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  in London. "The market forces are going to prevail. I've yet to see a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that will be credible enough to generate fear on the part of emerging market investors betting for weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Romania is another candidate for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although it hasn't done so yet despite the leu falling to its weakest level against the euro since late October. It is down 3% from the beginning of June.\par \par \uc2 "Emerging markets enter this week vulnerable, with the potential for markets to test policy makers further in terms of their willingness to act," said Gillian Edgeworth, chief emerging Europe, Middle East and Africa economist at \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  in London. "In Romania we have been surprised by the absence of the \uc2 National Bank of Romania\uc2  from the market, particularly given such a large move in the Romania leu against the euro."\par \par \uc2 Write to Patryk Wasilewski at patryk.wasilewski@dowjones.com and Clare Connaghan at clare.connaghan@dowjones.com [ 06-10-13 1111ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020130610e96a0003p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
