8 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CZECH REPUBLIC: The Czech government will meet its goal to lower its budget deficit below 3% of the country's total economic output this year despite floods wreaking havoc across many areas last week and heavy thunderstorms causing localized flash floods over the weekend, Prime Minister Petr Necas said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We will stick to our strategy to maintain the deficit of public finances at below 3%," Mr. Necas said Sunday in a live interview on the Czech public television news broadcaster CT24.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 POLAND\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may again \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to limit the Polish zloty's volatility, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Marek Belka told state news agency PAP late Friday, hours after the bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market for the first time since December 2011.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HUNGARY: Hungary's flood defenses held firm on Sunday morning as central Europe's worst floods in a decade moved through the northwest of the country toward the capital Budapest.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thousands of emergency workers, troops and volunteers in Germany battled the flooding on Sunday which have forced evacuations and which one politician termed a "national catastrophe."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROMANIA: Romania's unemployment rate edged down to 5.03% in May, from 5.29% a month earlier, the country's employment agency \f28 \uc2 \f2 ANOFM\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday, news agency Mediafax reports. In May 2012, the unemployment rate was 4.9%, \f28 \uc2 \f2 ANOFM\f28 \uc2 \f2  data showed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Marynia Kruk at marynia.kruk@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Go to \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/emergingeurope}}}\uc2 \f2  for the WSJ blog on Central and Eastern Europe, covering business, politics, society and more, written by our correspondents across the region.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 09, 2013 22:04 ET (02:04 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130610e96a0004w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
