\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Poland May Take Further Zloty Action\b0\par\par\uc2 220 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2013\par 02:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par C6\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    (FROM THE WALL STREET JOURNAL 6/10/13) \par    By Patryk Wasilewski \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WARSAW -- \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Poland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may again \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in order to limit the Polish zloty's volatility, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Marek Belka told state news agency PAP late Friday, hours after the bank stepped into the market for the first time since December 2011.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday took the market by surprise as it came only two days after the governor said the recent zloty weakening is a welcome trend as it helps the slowing economy regain competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 "We never preannounce these things, and if someone thought that we will not do it, then I am sorry, but we do not act in the interest of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market speculators," Mr. Belka said. "Somebody thought he will make money on the zloty weakening and got burned."\par \par \uc2 As a result, the zloty strengthened against the euro to about 4.23 from above 4.30 before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Belka explained Friday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's goal wasn't to defend some specific zloty level, but rather curb recent zloty volatility that pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a weakest level in a year against the euro on Thursday.\par \par \